{"id": "EUVD-2026-86731", "enisaUuid": "427acd37-283a-3cba-94b0-22d29b36e8e9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nieee802154: cc2520: fix FIFOP work use-after-free\n\nThe FIFOP interrupt handler queues cc2520_fifop_irqwork.  On removal,\ncc2520_remove() only flushes the work.  The devm-managed FIFOP IRQ\nremains active until after ->remove() returns and can queue the work\nagain after that flush, allowing it to run after the private data is\nreleased.\n\nDisable the work with disable_work_sync() instead of flushing it, so\nthe handler can no longer queue it once removal begins.  Destroy the\nbuffer mutex last, since the worker and the stop callback invoked\nthrough ieee802154_unregister_hw() both take it.\n\nFound by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:53:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4a1ba62a486a4c43af91d01661a95e82dc4aaefa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/56a9919d8494fb118eebf167bef0622528fbf2e7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c68fd52c73b676aee67020011e98fea125a978f4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/890a80d516a1447db5c21bf92841a82914ea897d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff5891b266a7fc6a062710836be84f1cc19338b5"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97600", "GHSA-rq9h-jcg5-92gp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03a1b44a-8540-3a7c-b329-704f3487e5e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "055dd3c4-d0a6-3afb-9f28-38584676a926", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "218b113a-3c93-30be-a021-8e4267f5fdb2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "53c916e4-cb37-335c-93cf-906e34d84717", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0da6bc8cc3417a5e452efb886ff2c61e72b743d6 <890a80d516a1447db5c21bf92841a82914ea897d"}, {"id": "5dbd1b86-0a5a-3f29-a51f-1d4fb6f4c138", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0da6bc8cc3417a5e452efb886ff2c61e72b743d6 <ff5891b266a7fc6a062710836be84f1cc19338b5"}, {"id": "5e03f8e5-12de-37a9-b121-01ce170987f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "b434f3dd-adb7-3387-a7a4-93502bebc648", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.17"}, {"id": "bcd34dd1-a447-3ea1-b1f5-f9023f33da4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "d27fcdeb-82bc-335a-8013-26500bf4dbb0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ea1ff8b4-bca9-38ae-a89e-4c66d9f8b751", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0da6bc8cc3417a5e452efb886ff2c61e72b743d6 <56a9919d8494fb118eebf167bef0622528fbf2e7"}, {"id": "f352edfe-c742-3519-8883-78e441afabd6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0da6bc8cc3417a5e452efb886ff2c61e72b743d6 <4a1ba62a486a4c43af91d01661a95e82dc4aaefa"}, {"id": "fa5d0eae-47ac-3c92-8144-5de207f5f49f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0da6bc8cc3417a5e452efb886ff2c61e72b743d6 <c68fd52c73b676aee67020011e98fea125a978f4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cceadfb0-d95a-36ed-b532-2d0600d899f4", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}